  "notes": "# DevClash 0.1.0-beta.4\n\nCloud sync is easier to find, understand and control, with a clearer on/off switch that stays visible on Linux as well as Mac and Windows.\n\n- When cloud sync is off, the dashboard offers **Enable Cloud Sync** and explains how eligible synced tokens can be converted into Build Credits in the web dashboard.\n- Account settings show a larger **On / Off** switch, describe what is uploaded, and follow the app's light or dark appearance.\n- Click the footer's cloud status to open settings. Off, pending, error and completed-sync states now have distinct indicators.\n- A failed preference change keeps the confirmed setting and lets you retry. Cloud uploads and public rankings remain separate choices.\n- Choose an owned project in your cloud account to assign new Claude, Codex and OpenCode usage until you switch or stop the project session. Cursor account-wide snapshots remain unassigned.\n- History uploads use batched server ingestion for less database work while preserving deduplication and recoverable progress.\n\nExisting preferences and optional cloud-sync consent are preserved. This remains a beta. Windows can show a SmartScreen reputation warning despite valid publisher signing. Linux native validation targets XFCE/X11; Wayland and physical Intel Mac coverage remain limited.\n\n- Simplified cloud account panel with expandable details and no large cloud header icon.\n- Sync status hover uses color and background feedback without an underline.\n\nBuilt locally on Mac, Linux and Windows. Desktop and signing inputs verified byte-for-byte against committed source 4d6ed0cf3f9a159373f6ac97f51523ed0bdc3d97.\n",
